      "content": "<p>Statement I : Dipole moment is a vector quantity and by convention it is depicted by a small arrow with tail on the negative centre and head pointing towards the positive centre.</p>\n<p>Statement II : The crossed arrow of the dipole moment symbolizes the direction of the shift of charges in the molecules.</p>\n<p>In the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below :</p>",
