      "explanation": "The dipole moment is a vector quantity and is\ndepicted by an arrow with tail on the positive centre\nand head pointing towards the negative centre. So,\nStatement-I is incorrect.<br><br> The crossed arrow of the\ndipole moment symbolizes the direction of the shift\nof charges in the molecules. So, Statement-II is\ncorrect.\n<br><br>For example,\n<br><br><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1lfhir5ak/bef2a348-5bc6-4420-b1b9-83b80f289fc8/86f105b0-c77f-11ed-ad62-0de788836124/file-1lfhir5al.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1lfhir5ak/bef2a348-5bc6-4420-b1b9-83b80f289fc8/86f105b0-c77f-11ed-ad62-0de788836124/file-1lfhir5al.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"JEE Main 2023 (Online) 25th January Evening Shift Chemistry - Chemical Bonding &amp; Molecular Structure Question 115 English Explanation\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1lfhir5ak/bef2a348-5bc6-4420-b1b9-83b80f289fc8/86f105b0-c77f-11ed-ad62-0de788836124/file-1lfhir5al.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1lfhir5ak/bef2a348-5bc6-4420-b1b9-83b80f289fc8/86f105b0-c77f-11ed-ad62-0de788836124/file-1lfhir5al.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1lfhir5ak/bef2a348-5bc6-4420-b1b9-83b80f289fc8/86f105b0-c77f-11ed-ad62-0de788836124/file-1lfhir5al.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1lfhir5ak/bef2a348-5bc6-4420-b1b9-83b80f289fc8/86f105b0-c77f-11ed-ad62-0de788836124/file-1lfhir5al.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1lfhir5ak/bef2a348-5bc6-4420-b1b9-83b80f289fc8/86f105b0-c77f-11ed-ad62-0de788836124/file-1lfhir5al.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1lfhir5ak/bef2a348-5bc6-4420-b1b9-83b80f289fc8/86f105b0-c77f-11ed-ad62-0de788836124/file-1lfhir5al.png?format=png